From: Paul Moses <p@1g4.org>
Subject: [PATCH] gtask: avoid storing a pre-cancellation error

Pre-cancelled return-on-cancel tasks still run their worker. Storing a
cancellation error at startup lets the worker overwrite that allocation
when it returns its own error. Check the cancellable without writing the
worker result slot, as the later cancellation path already does.

Return-on-cancel requires check-cancellable, so propagation still reports
cancellation. Extend the existing async and sync cancellation tests by
returning an error from the cancelled worker.

diff --git a/gio/gtask.c b/gio/gtask.c
--- a/gio/gtask.c
+++ b/gio/gtask.c
@@ -1641,8 +1641,7 @@
   if (task->cancellable)
     {
       if (task->return_on_cancel &&
-          g_cancellable_set_error_if_cancelled (task->cancellable,
-                                                &task->error))
+          g_cancellable_is_cancelled (task->cancellable))
         {
           task->thread_cancelled = task->thread_complete = TRUE;
           TRACE (GIO_TASK_AFTER_RUN_IN_THREAD (task, task->thread_cancelled));
diff --git a/gio/tests/task.c b/gio/tests/task.c
--- a/gio/tests/task.c
+++ b/gio/tests/task.c
@@ -1593,7 +1593,11 @@
       g_task_return_int (task, magic);
     }
   else
-    *state = THREAD_CANCELLED;
+    {
+      *state = THREAD_CANCELLED;
+      g_task_return_new_error (task, G_IO_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_FAILED,
+                               "Task failed after cancellation");
+    }
 
   g_cond_signal (&roc_finish_cond);
   g_mutex_unlock (&roc_finish_mutex);
